# Cross-platform provenance for hash-pinned scientific inputs.
#
# src/adaptive_qmix/provenance.py hashes the checked-out bytes of the frozen
# qualification network and refuses to run when they differ from the SHA-256
# recorded in config/adaptive_qmix/qualification_300m_medium.json. Under
# core.autocrlf=true a Windows checkout rewrites all 341 line endings to CRLF,
# which changes those bytes and therefore the digest, even though the file
# content and its Git blob identity are unchanged. Pinning the checkout to LF
# keeps the working-tree bytes identical on every platform.
#
# This affects the byte representation only. Do not change the network
# contents, its Git blob, or the frozen SHA-256 in the configuration.
sumo_scenarios/two_intersections/corridor_2x2/corridor_2x2.net.xml text eol=lf
